(text "5 V input (always on): fuse, TVS, reverse-polarity FET" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 13.97 15.748 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b3fdfd64-1856-5218-b0ee-76b2eea3b95b"))
(text "Q1 conducts through its body diode, then turns fully on (gate at 0 V). Reversed input: Q1 stays off." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 49.53 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "87acccd5-1fcd-5340-bc86-0b74e56f9998"))
(text "3V3_AO: always-on rail for the RTC, secure element and power control" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 13.97 56.388 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "04c63fe8-b699-5f7b-8b98-b3f9a0d61389"))
(text "XC6206: 1 uA quiescent, 6 V max input." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 88.9 66.04 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "62a9f1e9-5d7e-5314-9d41-2a31e42e8102"))
(text "Load: RTC, ATECC608C, pull-ups (uA)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 88.9 69.215 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "fd4827c6-047c-51bf-9b5f-d8ec10335c52"))
(text "Power control: EN_PWR = power button | RTC alarm | PWR_HOLD (FPGA)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 13.97 81.788 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "efcdbe86-89d8-5749-a4f5-1c82498af2a6"))
(text "Start: SW1 or the RTC /INT pulls PWR_ON_N low, Q2 charges EN_PWR.\nPower-on: C on PWR_ON_N gives one start pulse when 5 V arrives.\nRun: the boot ROM drives PWR_HOLD high. Sleep: the loader sets the\nnext alarm and drops PWR_HOLD; EN_PWR decays in about 2 s (2u2 x 1M)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 78.74 123.19 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "5e39386b-f3b3-5f13-9ff3-89e075a96f42"))
(text "Step-down converters, sequenced 1V0 -> 1V8 -> 3V3 through the power-good chain" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 13.97 132.588 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "718e22d3-cd76-5a8d-bafa-5c9a879f4da1"))
(text "1.0 V core (VCC, VCC_DRM): 0.6 V x (1 + 20k/30k)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 137.16 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1a94d829-9cf1-550f-b2c2-34f6b2d19ee5"))
(text "1.8 V auxiliary (VCCA, VCCADC): 0.6 V x (1 + 20k/10k)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 165.1 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0b6c50b0-0306-529d-abdc-3fcdeb8f7831"))
(text "3.3 V I/O and peripherals: 0.6 V x (1 + 68k/15k) = 3.32 V" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 193.04 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "fc0e9831-08de-589e-9638-f7df96c64e56"))
(text "5V_SW: 5 V for the speaker, backlight and sensor port, on when PGOOD" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 13.97 236.728 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c7b92571-aef0-5e1a-a4d0-a5a24cbaf79c"))
(text "FPGA core and auxiliary supplies, decoupling per UG040012 Table 2-3" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 143.51 15.748 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "604e2090-7abd-5e73-9f9e-870f575deedb"))
(text "VCC (14 balls): 3x100u, 6x4u7, 8x470n, 5x100n" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 149.86 78.105 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ed281167-aef6-5f16-9f9a-2751b9f4ed9c"))
(text "VCC_DRM (3 balls): 1x100u, 2x470n, 2x100n" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 149.86 136.525 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9b055196-d281-5c4a-b8b4-fbd66735c56f"))
(text "VCCA (5 balls): 1x47u, 3x4u7, 5x470n, 2x100n" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 223.52 78.105 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e32f534c-d804-5b9f-8abe-4401ed812bef"))
(text "VCCIOL6 (5 balls, no I/O bonded out): reduced set" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 223.52 118.745 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "04cd74b9-2e26-5c8e-b541-d3feef5c3537"))
(text "FPGA ground and no-connect balls" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 300.99 15.748 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "83c4d3ab-d787-5def-8be2-930d2857a964"))
(text "Notes\n1. 5 V is always present. 3V3_AO is always on; everything else is off in deep sleep.\n2. EN_PWR starts U3; each power-good output enables the next converter (UG040012 2.1:\n   follow the data sheet power-up order; core first, I/O last).\n3. PGOOD (3V3 in regulation) goes to the FPGA as a supply monitor input and switches 5V_SW.\n4. VCC and VCC_DRM share the 1.0 V supply (UG040012 2.3.1).\n5. Capacitor sizes: Table 2-6 calls for 1210 (100u, 47u) and 0805 (4u7); 1206 and 0603\n   parts from the JLCPCB basic list are used here. Place 470n/100n under the BGA.\n6. TLV62569P: 2 A, 1.5 MHz, 2.2 uH. Check the 1.0 V load with Pango Power Planner." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 144.78 200.66 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0d983df3-e900-5025-abe9-ec01320afdfd"))
